Z||000002||gomobile||10-16-2001||03:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fpc777:<BR><B>I have a high speed shake in my fiero<BR>when I get up to about 70mph the car starts shaking all over the road.<BR>I don't want to spend 100 or 1000 of dollars<BR>to fix a small problem<BR>please some idea's on what it might be<P>thank you for your time<BR>frank</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>1) U might need to get all wheel's balance?2) Rotate them if you haven't.<BR>2) Make sure and check DOG_BONE cause the<BR>bushings could be BAD!<P><BR>||||reg||6
Z||000003||Pheagey||10-16-2001||03:45 PM||||   I agree. Before I had my tires changed I would shack like crazy and didn't feel safe over 70MPH. After words I've now pushed 100 with no problem (and I need shocks).<BR>   If a balance/alignment doesn't do it chec ball joints and bushings, etc.||||reg||6
Z||000004||Patrick86GT||10-16-2001||06:20 PM||||all good advice<P>also, check the steering damper||||reg||1
Z||000005||dcaprio||10-16-2001||08:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fpc777:<BR><B>I have a high speed shake in my fiero<BR>when I get up to about 70mph the car starts shaking all over the road.<BR>I don't want to spend 100 or 1000 of dollars<BR>to fix a small problem<BR>please some idea's on what it might be<P>thank you for your time<BR>frank</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR> <BR>I had the same problem with my 84 coup. I tried all the above and still had a slight shake at 70 mph. I just got used to it. I switched the nose to an aero nose and the shake went away. I would first check all the other solutions first.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Zoom88||10-16-2001||09:40 PM||||<FONT COLOR="blue"> Just my 2 cents.....may be the inner tie-rod bushing. If you cut the wheel hard to the left do you here a popping noise ? (try this at a very slow speed maybe in a parking lot or such). Anyway my 88 does the same thing I ordered a bushing and tie-rod from Rodney just waiting on some time to replace it !!</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Zoom88 (edited 10-16-2001).]||||reg||1
